 "scope": "Item 5b: on-die termination trim for the wired RX/USB pad (wirepad), schematic-on-extraction study.\nThe drawn termination per leg is 8 x 20 um nfet_03v3 switches (TERM_GATE_x) in series with a 16/1.3 ppolyf_u\nstrap to TERM_VCM: 46 / 53 / 40 ohm (tt/ss/ff), i.e. switch-dominated. Trim = split the switch into a base\nsection (always on with TERM_ENABLE) plus 4 binary sections (TERM_TRIM[3:0]): W = 105 + 7.5*k um (k = 0..15).\nHere each code is emulated by scaling the eight extracted switch devices of each leg to W/8 (geometry\nparasitics of the extra width are not drawn yet). Bench = stress_safe_usb 'term' (8.9 mA into PAD_P,\nR = (V(PAD_P) - VCM) / 8.9 mA) at TERM_VCM 0 / 1.0 V, and 'cap' (all off) for the maximum-W case.\n    python3 termtrim.py <out.json>",
